    {
      "chunkIndex": 3,
      "contentPreview": "TEST-DESIGN LESSON: when a test\u0027s premise is \u0027a write leaves the cache warm\u0027, don\u0027t just assert on read CONTENT afterward \u2014 content can be correct via an unrelated cold-load path (e.g. LoadIndexUnsafe\u0027s independent AttributeMigration.MigratesTo forward-fill) even when the cache never actually got populated by the write under test, silently making the test assert nothing about the write path. Prove the read is a genuine cache HIT first: delete the scope\u0027s \u0027.lock\u0027 file, run the read, assert the lo",
